{"QuestionText":"In the main part of the survey, we are going to ask you to use a slider to evaluate the functions of different kinds of \"ideal relationships.\" When we say an \"ideal relationship,\" we mean <b>the <i>best relationship<\/i> that individuals could have with one another (in terms of a relationship of that kind).<br><\/b>\n<br>\n<span style=\"color:#e74c3c;\"><strong>You did not answer correctly again.<\/strong><\/span> For the purposes of this survey, what would be an \"ideal relationship\" between two siblings?","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Good_3","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"In the main part of the survey, we are going to ask you to use a slider to evaluate the functions...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"The worst relationship that a parent and child could have (for a relationship of that kind)"},"2":{"Display":"The average relationship that a parent and child could have (for a relationship of that kind)"},"3":{"Display":"The best relationship that a parent and child could have (for a relationship of that kind)"},"4":{"Display":"The most typical relationship that a parent and child could have (for a relationship of that kind)"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"RequestResponse","ForceResponseType":"RequestResponse","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":6,"QuestionID":"QID1046","DisplayLogic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1045\/SelectableChoice\/1","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In the main part of the survey, we are going to ask you how much an \"ideal\" relationship of a given type should serve the 4 functions you learned about.\n\nWhen we say an \"ideal relationship,\" we mea...<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">The worst relationship a parent and child could have (for a relationship of that kind)<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1045\/SelectableChoice\/1","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1045","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1045","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"1":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1045\/SelectableChoice\/2","Conjuction":"Or","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">Or<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In the main part of the survey, we are going to ask you how much an \"ideal\" relationship of a given type should serve the 4 functions you learned about.\n\nWhen we say an \"ideal relationship,\" we mea...<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">The average relationship a parent and child could have (for a relationship of that kind)<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1045\/SelectableChoice\/2","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1045","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1045","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"2":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1045\/SelectableChoice\/4","Conjuction":"Or","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">Or<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In the main part of the survey, we are going to ask you how much an \"ideal\" relationship of a given type should serve the 4 functions you learned about.\n\nWhen we say an \"ideal relationship,\" we mea...<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">The most typical relationship a parent and child could have (for a relationship of that kind)<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1045\/SelectableChoice\/4","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1045","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1045","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression","inPage":false}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_8HUAhazmhLBaak6","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1047","SecondaryAttribute":"Click to write the question text","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Click to write the question text","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q454","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Click to write the question text","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID1047"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_8HUAhazmhLBaak6","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1048","SecondaryAttribute":"Function 2 \/ 4: Transaction is for balancing mutual benefits by keeping track of who owes what to...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Function 2 \/ 4:<br><br>\n\n\n<p><b>Transaction<\/b> is for <u>balancing mutual benefits by keeping track of who owes what to whom<\/u>.&nbsp;<\/p><p><br><\/p><p>This function coordinates behavior in situations where individuals <u>do not<\/u> have a special responsibility for helping each other unconditionally, but when they can still mutually benefit through cooperation or exchange.&nbsp;<\/p><p><br><\/p><p>This can also be referred to as \"tit-for-tat\" behavior.<br><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"TransDef","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Function 2 \/ 4: Transaction is for balancing mutual benefits by keeping track of who owes what to...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID1048"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_8HUAhazmhLBaak6","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1049","SecondaryAttribute":"Function 3 \/ 4: Hierarchy is for coordinating behavior between individuals with unequal authority...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Function 3 \/ 4:<br>\n<br>\n<b>Hierarchy<\/b> is for coordinating behavior between <u>individuals with unequal authority<\/u> over one another.<br>\n<br>\nIn many situations, it is most effective for one individual to be in charge or have \"final say\" about what happens.<br>\n<br>\nSo, the hierarchy function involves assigning individuals roles based on their respective authority and responsibility in a given situation, in order to coordinate behavior in a more efficient manner and help accomplish goals.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"HierDef","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Function 3 \/ 4: Hierarchy is for coordinating behavior between individuals with unequal authority...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID1049"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_8HUAhazmhLBaak6","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1050","SecondaryAttribute":"Function 4 \/ 4: Mating\u00a0is for establishing a sexual or romantic relationship. For our ancestors,...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Function 4 \/ 4:\n<br><br><b>Mating<\/b>&nbsp;is for establishing a sexual or romantic relationship. <br><br>For our ancestors, the ultimate point of mating was to produce healthy offspring, so that we could pass on our genes and continue as a species. <br><br>Of course, today we have birth control, and people often have sexual or romantic relationships without consciously planning to have children. <br><br>But the underlying \"logic\" of the mating function \u00ad\u00adin terms of the <u>feelings and motivations<\/u> it tends to inspire remains the same: to attract and secure an intimate partner.\n\n&nbsp;","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"MateDef","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Function 4 \/ 4: Mating\u00a0is for establishing a sexual or romantic relationship. For our ancestors,...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID1050"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_8HUAhazmhLBaak6","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1051","SecondaryAttribute":"Here is the final practice. This training is to make sure you understand how to use the scale in...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Here is the final practice. This training is to make sure you understand how to use the scale in the main part of the study.<br>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q458","QuestionID":"QID1051","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Here is the final practice. This training is to make sure you understand how to use the scale in...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_8HUAhazmhLBaak6","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1052","SecondaryAttribute":"Practice 1 \/ 1:\u00a0 This is a practice trial so you can get used to the kind of question we will ask..","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p>Practice 1 \/ 1:&nbsp;<\/p><p><i><br><\/i><\/p><p><i>This is a practice trial so you can get used to the kind of question we will ask you<\/i>.<\/p><p><br><\/p><p>-------------------<\/p><p><br><\/p><p>Please consider an <u>ideal&nbsp;relationship<\/u> between <b>a parent and young child.<\/b><br>\n<br>\nThis refers to biological or adoptive parents and their young children (under the age of 18).&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<br><\/p>\n\n\n<p>For each of the functions below, please move the slider to show how much you think an <u style=\"\">ideal<\/u><u>&nbsp;relationship<\/u> of this kind should serve that function.&nbsp;<\/p><p><br><\/p><p><b>Note<\/b>: If you think it doesn't matter or it's neutral whether the relationship should serve that function, please select \"0\".<\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q459","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Practice 1 \/ 1:\u00a0 This is a practice trial so you can get used to the kind of question we will ask...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID1052"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_8HUAhazmhLBaak6","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1053","SecondaryAttribute":"Should this relationship be characterized by giving or receiving support based on need and abilit...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Should this relationship be characterized by <b>giving or receiving support based on need and ability<\/b> without creating a sense of debt or expecting something specific in return (i.e., with \"no strings attached\")? (Care function)<br><br>Specifically, should the <u>Parent<\/u> behave in a supportive manner (with \"no strings attached\") toward their <u>Child<\/u>?<br>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"slider_1","QuestionType":"Slider","Selector":"HSLIDER","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","CSSliderMin":-100,"CSSliderMax":100,"GridLines":2,"SnapToGrid":false,"NumDecimals":"0","ShowValue":true,"CustomStart":true,"SliderStartPositions":{"1":0.5011655011655011815463467428344301879405975341796875,"4":0.5},"NotApplicable":false,"MobileFirst":true},"QuestionDescription":"Should this relationship be characterized by giving or receiving support based on need and abilit...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Should the <u>Parent<\/u> behave in a supportive manner (with \"no strings attached\") toward their <u>Child<\/u>?"},"4":{"Display":"Should the <u>Child<\/u> behave in a supportive manner (with \"no strings attached\") toward their <u>Parent<\/u>?"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","4"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"RequestResponse","ForceResponseType":"RequestResponse","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":7,"Labels":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely SHOULD NOT"},"2":{"Display":"Neutral"},"6":{"Display":"Definitely SHOULD"}},"QuestionID":"QID1053"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_8HUAhazmhLBaak6","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1054","SecondaryAttribute":"How should you respond if you think it doesn't matter or it's neutral whether the relationship sh...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"How should you respond if you think it doesn't matter or it's neutral whether the relationship should serve a given function?<br>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"neutral_1","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"How should you respond if you think it doesn't matter or it's neutral whether the relationship sh...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Select \"Definitely should\" (4)"},"2":{"Display":"Select \"Neutral\" (0)"},"3":{"Display":"Select anywhere on the scale"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID1054"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_8HUAhazmhLBaak6","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1055","SecondaryAttribute":"You answered incorrectly. How should you respond if you \"think it doesn't matter or it's neutral...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<span style=\"color:#e74c3c;\"><strong>You answered incorrectly. <\/strong><\/span>How should you respond if you &quot;think it doesn&#39;t matter or it&#39;s neutral whether the relationship should serve that function&quot;?","DefaultChoices":